dash='## Quant & Market Dashboard\n\n### Liquidity and volatility\n\n- **Overnight:** Futures show technology weakness at 04:32 CST. Current ES/NQ spreads, depth, overnight volume, ETF NBBO and Treasury depth are unverified. Treat direction as a cautious sentiment proxy, not a liquidity rating. Refresh the execution feed as fixed-income trading resumes after Veterans Day; do not infer measured depth recovery.\n- **Funding:** Latest verified SOFR is 3.88% for November 9, updated November 10 at 07:02 CST. FRED lists November 12 as the next release; the new update was unavailable at cutoff. This lagged fixing does not diagnose current stress. [FRED](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/SOFR).\n- **Regime: Moderate; medium confidence.** Delayed VIX was 18.29 at November 12 06:38 EST / 05:38 CST, versus November 11 close 17.49. House bands: below 15 low, 15–25 moderate, 25–35 high, above 35 stressed; descriptive, not calibrated forecasts. Skew, term structure and dealer gamma are unverified. [VIX](https://chartexchange.com/symbol/index-vix/historical/).\n\n### Factor proxies\n\n| Factor | ETF | Nov 10→11 | Oct 9→Nov 11 (~1 month) |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n| Momentum | [MTUM](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/mtum/history/) | +3.79% | -13.42% |\n| Value | [VLUE](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/vlue/history/) | +2.95% | -3.57% |\n| Quality | [QUAL](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/qual/history/) | +0.97% | -0.69% |\n| Size | [IWM](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/iwm/history/) | +0.89% | +1.49% |\n| Growth | [IWF](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/iwf/history/) | +2.28% | -8.83% |\n| Low volatility | [SPLV](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/splv/history/) | +0.14% | +8.40% |\n\nSource-linked split-adjusted Close-column price returns, excluding distributions, through November 11 at 16:00 EST / 15:00 CST. October 9 baselines are archived from the prior edition; latest closes were rechecked today. These are imperfect ETF proxies, not isolated factor premia. Corporate actions were not independently validated. All six rose Wednesday; momentum and growth remain negative over the longer window while size and low volatility remain positive.\n\n### Execution and microstructure\n\n- Cash opening auction: 08:30 CST / 14:30 UTC today. October PPI is scheduled Friday November 13 at 07:30 CST / 13:30 UTC; results unknown. Recheck other release and speaker calendars before staging orders. [BLS calendar](https://www.bls.gov/schedule/2026/11_sched_list.htm).\n- SPY/QQQ: inspect quote age, NBBO spreads, depth, auction imbalances and ES/NQ basis. Use bounded limits and participation caps; stress slippage, gaps, cancellations, missed fills and latency. Yesterday’s rally can become a liquidity trap if displayed depth vanishes.\n- Options: verify same-day expiry availability, deliverables and settlement, and Friday expiry exposure. Reject stale, crossed or one-sided quotes. Near-expiry gamma and event-related volatility repricing matter, but dealer-gamma sign, expiry concentrations, pinning and flow magnitude remain unknown.\n\n**Research watchlist:** SPY, QQQ, IWM, RSP, TLT; ES, NQ, ZN, VX; MTUM, VLUE, QUAL, IWF, SPLV; NVDA, IBM, GOOGL.\n\n### DRL Improvements for the MATLAB System\n\n1. Enforce drawdown, exposure, participation and stale-data limits outside the policy, with an explicit safe fallback.\n2. Penalize spread, impact, turnover, latency and missed fills; compare forecast magnitude with the full cost hurdle before acting.\n3. Use purged walk-forward evaluation, training-only preprocessing and a one-use final holdout; hold out assets and regimes separately.\n4. Randomize depth, observation delays and fill probabilities; test abstention when predicted advantage is smaller than cost uncertainty.\n\n### Model hygiene\n\nAudit leakage, survivorship bias, look-ahead, corporate actions, stale options quotes, multiple testing, calibration and drift. Preserve point-in-time universes, release vintages and availability timestamps. Fit preprocessing inside folds. Daily OHLCV cannot recreate Level-3 queues or validate sub-second fills.\n\n### MATLAB optimization patterns\n\n- Use named-zone timetables and causal synchronization; retain quote and event timestamps separately.\n- Vectorize rolling features, preallocate logs and profile bottlenecks.\n- Parallelize independent folds or Bayesian trials with reproducible random streams and fixed budgets.\n- Use GPUs for sufficiently large batches; keep forecasts, execution simulation and risk controls modular.\n\n### High-value quant research question\n\n**Does a calibrated forecast-versus-cost abstention gate improve net execution quality over the same predictor without the gate under realistic latency and missed fills?**\n\nUse matched seeds, risk budgets and action opportunities across held-out regimes. This tests whether predictive accuracy can improve decisions once spread, fees, impact and fill uncertainty are included.\n'
